[ ] Fix the edit-time hook that reformats Rust files non-canonically $An edit-time hook in the agent harness (not this repo — .githooks/pre-commit is check-only) reformats edited source files into a non-canonical style between turns. Five incidents: runs 5 and 7 (twice, identical 10-insertion/20-deletion diff each time) on tests/walking_skeleton.rs, and run 9 on .pi/extensions/agent-workspace/index.ts and index.test.ts (whitespace-only line-wrapping collapse). Impact is absorbed on three levels for Rust: git checkout restores the committed canonical form, the pre-commit fmt gate rejects it from commits, and rustfmt-normalized fingerprints keep observations and claims current through the byte drift. TypeScript has no such gate: the hook only sees .rs files, so .ts drift is invisible to every automated layer and is caught only by git diff -w review and manual restoration. Fix at the source: configure or disable the harness edit-time formatter so it either runs the file's canonical formatter (rustfmt for .rs, prettier/biome for .ts if adopted) or leaves files alone. Verify by editing a .rs and a .ts test file and confirming the working tree stays clean between turns.$ !5 +environment ^2026-09-01T19:18 #01a05fe9-40b4-7880-b405-ce1fbc0d8820
